{
 "id": "motion_cloak",
 "label": "Motion Cloak",
 "category": "Time",
 "tags": [
  "look"
 ],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The invisibility cloak from the films, worked out from the movement. Whatever moves turns into living glass: you see the street behind a walker straight through them, bent and rippled by their outline and by the folds of their clothes, with a thin bright edge where the light catches. The view behind is rebuilt from the moments before and after they cover it, so it really is the background, not a blur. When they stop they slowly come back into view. Works best with a camera that holds still or pans gently.",
